  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_wey_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>wey, a measure of weight, usually equal to twelve stone or c. 300 lb. (OED s.v. waw, n.2, wey1; Zupko 434-8), used for dry goods including salt, cheese, glass, tallow, sheep tallow (cepum moltonis), butter, thrumes, and battery; as a packing unit for glass containing 60 bunches (also 60 bunches for Renishe window glass), and for salt containing 40 bushels; note 7 centene = 80 vagas | clearly some kind of measure of salt, but exact meaning unknown</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
